Now add encounter seenScp toast in spawnEnemyAround. Later.

Menu functions. Need implement. Let's add after hideScreens maybe. Also update hideScreens to include dock. Current:
```
function hideScreens(except) {
 [menu, pause, dawn, over].forEach... 
}
```
Add `DOM.menuDock.classList.add('hidden')`? hideScreens used in init(hideScreens(DOM.menuScreen)) and startGame(hideScreens()). In startGame, hide dock yes. In init hideScreens(menu) should hide dock but menu is shown. We'll manage.

Add functions:
```
function menuIsOpen() { return !DOM.menuScreen.classList.contains('hidden'); }
function refreshMenuButtons() { setText(DOM.startBtn, game.runActive ? 'New Run' : 'Start Game'); DOM.resumeMenuBtn.hidden = !game.runActive || game.mode==='menu'; ... }
function openMenu() {
 if (game.mode === 'playing') { togglePause(); } // pause screen shows, hide it
 if (game.mode === 'paused' || game.mode==='dawn'...) ...
 hideScreens(DOM.menuScreen);
 DOM.pauseScreen.classList.add('hidden');
 DOM.menuScreen.classList.remove('hidden','minimized');
 DOM.menuDock.classList.add('hidden');
 DOM.resumeMenuBtn.hidden = !game.runActive;
 setText start New Run if runActive...
 Sound.ui();
}
function closeMenu() {
 if (DOM.menuScreen.classList.contains('hidden')) return;
 DOM.menuScreen.classList.add('hidden');
 DOM.menuScreen.classList.remove('minimized');
 DOM.menuDock.classList.add('hidden');
 if (game.mode === 'paused') resumeGame();
 else if (game.mode === 'menu') {
   // closed terminal: world idle; show dock
   DOM.menuDock.classList.remove('hidden');
   setText(DOM.menuDockLabel, 'NIGHTFALL');
   // maybe start? No.
 }
}
function minimizeMenu() {
 if (game.mode==='menu') { // idle
   DOM.menuScreen.classList.add('minimized');
   DOM.menuDock.classList.remove('hidden');
   setText(...);
 } else {
   // whenever menu open during paused, minimize and keep paused? Should resume? "minimize" likely keeps paused.
   DOM.menuScreen.classList.add('minimized');
   DOM.menuDock.classList.remove('hidden');
 }
}
function expandMenu() {
 DOM.menuScreen.classList.remove('hidden','minimized');
 DOM.menuDock.classList.add('hidden');
 hideScreens(DOM.menuScreen);
}
```
But when game.mode==='paused' and menu open, underlying pause screen should be hidden. openMenu: if playing call togglePause() (sets paused, shows pause screen), then hide pause screen. Good. On close, resume. During minimize if game.mode paused, pause screen hidden; dock shown. Clicking dock expand menu. Good.
When initial menu minimized/closed, game.mode='menu'. If dock click expand. If initial menu close, show dock; that's okay, no HUD. Maybe also show a floating "Start" in dock? The dock label "NIGHTFALL / OPEN MENU", fine.
Resume button: in menu, if runActive show "Resume Run" and clicking calls closeMenu; since game.mode paused -> resume. If game.mode became menu (not started) hidden.
Pause menu button: openMenu() while paused.
HUD menu button: openMenu() if playing. If paused, openMenu? HUD button is behind pause overlay; no.
